# Ollama Modelfile for the local "voice-agent" model.
#
# Build it from the repository root:
#     ollama create voice-agent -f models/Modelfile
# The GGUF is not in git (see .gitignore); keep it in this folder.
#
# No TEMPLATE override: Ollama reads the chat template embedded in the GGUF.
# UNVERIFIED on this project's machine (Ollama is not installed there): that the installed Ollama loads this
# architecture, that it picks up the embedded template, and how to switch thinking off for this model.
# Check with `ollama run voice-agent "Say hello in one sentence."` before relying on it: if the reply starts with
# reasoning, thinking is on.
#
# Thinking is NOT disabled by this file or by the request. The client's ThinkFilter (llm/client.py) is the only
# defence, and it is partial: it removes a complete <think>...</think> block, and reasoning that ends with a
# </think> inside the first 120 characters of a reply (ThinkFilter.LEAD_HOLD_CHARS). Longer reasoning is spoken.
# Reasoning also spends the 300-token reply budget. Turning thinking off here is the real fix once it is verified.
FROM ./Qwen3.5-4B-Uncensored-HauhauCS-Aggressive-Q4_K_M.gguf
PARAMETER num_ctx 2048
